Z||000000||84sleepr||12-01-2001||09:19 PM||||I've been still having trouble with stalling after the car reaches operating temperature at a stop sign or light.<P>My car is a 84 SE, automatic.  <P>I scanned it last week and replaced the coolant temp sensor - code 15.  However the car still stalls at operating temp at a stop.<P>The check engine light usually breifly appears and then goes away so I scanned it again and ... code 15-low coolant temp.<P>Would this most likly be a wiring problem between the sensor and the ECM?  How should I go about replairing the problem?  <P>Please help, the car is pretty much perfect except for this annoying problem!||||reg||5
Z||000001||frankshel||12-01-2001||10:28 PM||||I would look for a vacuum leak first. If it is running at regular speeds with no problems, and only stalls when stopping, I would alsmost bet there is a vacuum leak in one of the hoses that attach to the carbeurator. Check that first...then look for an injector problem....remove the breather and the injector...clean the injector and then give it a try.<BR>Frank Sheldon<BR>Albany, NY ||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||12-02-2001||12:54 PM||||Did you replace the guage sensor. or did you replace the ecm sensor? There usually is two different sensors. The guage one generally uses a green wire, and the ecm generally has a yellow wire to/at sensor, Both should be close to the t/stat.  Be sure you replaced the ecm one. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||84sleepr||12-02-2001||02:08 PM||||Yeah, I made sure I replaced the ECM one.<P>There's one in the t-stat pipe and one in the manifold I believe a few inches away.  I replaced the one in the manifold.<BR>||||reg||1
